#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_p2p_in_chat.html.heex:29
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Messages during the session are regular private messages, saved like any other. Session events — connected, file received, game score, who ended it — are written into the PM history as P2P lines, so the story of the session survives it. While connected, the PM tab shows a small P2P icon."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_channel_conference.html.heex:80
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Moderation"
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_p2p_in_chat.html.heex:22
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Once connected, the P2P menu in the menu bar (mirrored in the Start menu) opens the session windows: Call for audio/video, Files for transfers, Games for the two-player arcade, and P2P Statistics for live telemetry. Windows auto-open on activity — an incoming file offer opens Files, a game proposal opens Games, and when your peer turns their camera or microphone on the Call window surfaces and you join automatically."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_universal_lobby.html.heex:9
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Once connected, the call starts automatically with each side's setup choices and the Files, Games and Statistics windows wait minimized on the taskbar. Everything runs concurrently over the same connection: share your screen, send a file during the call, start a game without hanging up. Ending any one activity never drops the others — only ending the session does."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_universal_lobby.html.heex:7
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "One Connection, Every Feature"
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_p2p_in_chat.html.heex:54
