#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Statistics"
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_p2p_in_chat.html.heex:43
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The Call window uses the same media language as channel conferences: mic, camera, screen share, devices, PiP, layout, self-view, mini mode, docked statistics and reaction controls are icon buttons with tooltips. End Call stops only the media; closing a P2P window asks before ending the whole P2P session."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_universal_lobby.html.heex:2
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The P2P Lobby is the persistent peer-to-peer connection behind /p2p: one link between two users that hosts a call, file transfers and games all at the same time. It lives inside the chat — setup happens before sending or accepting the invite, and accepting opens the session windows right on the chat desktop, next to your conversations."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_network_stats.html.heex:2
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The P2P Statistics window shows live telemetry for the whole P2P session: WebRTC connection, audio, video or screen source, file transfer and game data channels. Click the ? button in the panel to see a short explanation of each metric inline, or hover any row for a tooltip."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_media_devices.html.heex:9
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The P2P setup dialog lists microphone, camera, and speaker choices before sending or accepting an invite. During an active call, open Devices from the Call toolbar to choose a different microphone, camera, or audio output."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_p2p_in_chat.html.heex:27
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The PM Is the Conversation"
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_p2p_in_chat.html.heex:20
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The Session Windows"
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_p2p_in_chat.html.heex:34
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The Status Bar Area"
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_channel_conference.html.heex:66
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The conference window shows explicit states while waiting for participants, joining receive-only, recovering media, or handling a failed connection. Recoverable failures keep the call open and expose Retry; leaving from a warning or error still uses the confirmation dialog so microphone, camera and SFU cleanup stay predictable."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_audio_call.html.heex:41
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The header and status bar show call duration, quality, active facets and relay privacy. The peer list is intentionally compact because P2P is always one-to-one."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_network_stats.html.heex:9
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The header shows the peer, session state, browser/WebRTC state, peer online state, active call/file/game facets and whether the privacy relay is active."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_channel_conference.html.heex:18
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The pre-join dialog lets you preview your camera, choose microphone, camera and speaker devices, and decide whether to join with microphone or camera enabled. Permission and device failures show a Retry action, and you can still join receive-only. Layout and media defaults are remembered for your account; browser-specific device choices are remembered locally."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_p2p_in_chat.html.heex:36
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The status bar always shows your active session, wherever you are in the chat. It also shows compact badges for active call, file transfer, game, call quality and relay privacy. Click it to bring the P2P windows to the front (or open Statistics when none is open); the stop button next to it cancels a pending invite or ends the session, after a confirmation."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_p2p_in_chat.html.heex:9
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Type /p2p <nick> (or use the nicklist context menu) to open setup before sending an invite. Confirming setup sends the invite card in the private message; the invited person clicks Accept to start their own setup and join in place, or Decline to refuse — the inviter is told either way."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_video_call.html.heex:16
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Use the layout controls for Auto, Focus, Split, Speaker and Compact views. Click the remote tile to focus it. The self-view button cycles your own video between tile, picture-in-picture and hidden."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_channel_conference.html.heex:58
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Use the reaction buttons in the conference toolbar to send a short visual reaction. Reactions are ephemeral, appear on participant tiles and rows, are not stored as chat messages, and are lightly rate limited to avoid spam."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_channel_conference.html.heex:42
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Use the screen share button in the conference toolbar to publish your selected screen or window. The shared screen replaces your outgoing camera video while it is active, becomes the focused conference tile, and returns to camera when you stop sharing or the browser ends capture."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_channel_conference.html.heex:10
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "When a channel has an active conference, the Call control shows a live badge with state, participant count and elapsed time. The info button opens a summary with participants, current speaker when available, media icons and a Join/Open action. Channel tabs and the conversations sidebar also show a compact conference glyph."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_channel_conference.html.heex:34
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "When a conference is active, use Ctrl+Shift+ArrowUp to mute or unmute your microphone, Ctrl+Shift+ArrowLeft to start or stop your camera, Ctrl+Shift+ArrowRight to cycle layouts, Ctrl+Shift+ArrowDown to focus the next participant, and Ctrl+Shift+Q to open the leave confirmation. Hold Ctrl+Shift+Z for push-to-talk while muted. Conference shortcuts do not fire from editable text fields."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_p2p_in_chat.html.heex:49
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "When the P2P Call window is focused, Ctrl+Shift media shortcuts control microphone, camera, layout, self-view, screen share and end-call media."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_p2p_in_chat.html.heex:63
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "When the server has a TURN relay configured, the setup dialog or Toggle Privacy Mode in the P2P menu can force the whole connection through the relay, so your IP address is never shared with your peer. The preference is remembered for future sessions."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_video_call.html.heex:22
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "With the P2P Call window focused, Ctrl+Shift+ArrowRight cycles layouts and Ctrl+Shift+ArrowDown cycles self-view."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_audio_call.html.heex:20
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "With the P2P Call window focused, Ctrl+Shift+ArrowUp toggles microphone state and Ctrl+Shift+ArrowLeft toggles camera state."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_p2p_in_chat.html.heex:56
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "You can hold one P2P session at a time. Accepting a new invite — or inviting someone else — while a session is active asks whether to end the current one first; any call, transfer or game in progress stops when you switch."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_audio_call.html.heex:28
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "to stop your media call. The P2P session remains available for private messages, files, games and statistics until you end the session itself."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_network_stats.html.heex:53
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "— resolution and frame rate of the received video or screen stream."
msgstr ""
